{"id":"leetcode-44","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Wildcard Matching","summary":"Implement wildcard pattern matching for a string (s) using a pattern (p) that includes '?' for any single character and '*' for any sequence of characters, including an empty sequence.","statement":"Implement wildcard pattern matching for a string (s) using a pattern (p) that includes '?' for any single character and '*' for any sequence of characters, including an empty sequence. Ensure the entire string (s) matches the pattern (p).","constraints":["s and p each have length 0–2000. s contains lowercase letters.","p contains lowercase letters, '?' (exactly one arbitrary character), and '*' (any sequence, possibly empty).","Match the entire string. A star acts independently, not on the preceding character."],"topics":["strings","dynamic-programming","recursion"],"prerequisites":["strings","dynamic-programming"],"signature":{"name":"wildcard_match","parameters":[{"name":"s","annotation":"str","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null},{"name":"p","annotation":"str","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"bool","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def wildcard_match(s: str, p: str) -> bool:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def wildcard_match(s, p):\n    previous = [False] * (len(p) + 1)\n    previous[0] = True\n    for j in range(1, len(p) + 1):\n        previous[j] = p[j - 1] == \"*\" and previous[j - 1]\n    for char in s:\n        current = [False] * (len(p) + 1)\n        for j in range(1, len(p) + 1):\n            if p[j - 1] == \"*\":\n                current[j] = current[j - 1] or previous[j]\n            else:\n                matches = p[j - 1] == \"?\" or p[j - 1] == char\n                current[j] = matches and previous[j - 1]\n        previous = current\n    return previous[-1]\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def wildcard_match(s, p):\n    previous = [False] * (len(p) + 1)\n    previous[0] = True\n    for j in range(1, len(p) + 1):\n        previous[j] = p[j - 1] == \"*\" and previous[j - 1]\n    for char in s:\n        current = [False] * (len(p) + 1)\n        for j in range(1, len(p) + 1):\n            if p[j - 1] == \"*\":\n                current[j] = previous[j]\n            else:\n                matches = p[j - 1] == \"?\" or p[j - 1] == char\n                current[j] = matches and previous[j - 1]\n        previous = current\n    return previous[-1]\n","def wildcard_match(s, p):\n    previous = [False] * (len(p) + 1)\n    previous[0] = True\n    for j in range(1, len(p) + 1):\n        previous[j] = p[j - 1] == \"*\" and previous[j - 1]\n    for char in s:\n        current = [False] * (len(p) + 1)\n        for j in range(1, len(p) + 1):\n            if p[j - 1] == \"*\":\n                current[j] = current[j - 1] or previous[j]\n            else:\n                matches = p[j - 1] == char\n                current[j] = matches and previous[j - 1]\n        previous = current\n    return previous[-1]\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(|s| × |p|)","target_space_complexity":"O(|p|)","estimated_minutes":50,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":3,"prerequisites":2,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":1},"hints":["Ask whether each text prefix matches each pattern prefix.","A star can either match nothing or consume another text character while staying on the same star.","For a star use current[j-1] or previous[j]; for a literal/question mark use the diagonal state and a one-character match.","Only a prefix made entirely of stars can match empty text. Question mark always consumes exactly one character."],"editorial":"In prefix DP, an independent star either advances only the pattern (empty match) or advances only the text (another consumed character). Other pattern characters consume one from each side and require literal equality or a question mark. Initialize the empty-text row through consecutive stars. Keeping only two rows limits auxiliary space to the pattern length. The independent oracle is fnmatchcase, whose whole-string semantics agree on this restricted grammar without brackets or other extensions.","tests":[{"id":"lc-44-1","arguments":["aa","a"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"A single literal a cannot cover the entire string aa.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-2","arguments":["adceb","*a*b"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The first star can be empty, a matches a, the second star covers dce, and b matches b.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-3","arguments":["",""],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-4","arguments":["","*"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-5","arguments":["","?"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-6","arguments":["a",""],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-7","arguments":["a","?"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-8","arguments":["aa","*"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-9","arguments":["cb","?a"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-10","arguments":["ab","a*b"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-11","arguments":["abc","a?c"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-12","arguments":["abc","***"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-13","arguments":["acdcb","a*c?b"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-14","arguments":["ab","*c"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-stress-1","arguments":["",""],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-44-stress-2","arguments":["",""],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null}],"variation_dimensions":[],"seed_problem_id":null,"prompt_version":null}
